  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong: all thermal incidents must be reported within 24 hours, with customer notice within 72 hours, and reporting continues during investigation. S2 keeps the 5% limit and gives customers exact per-model failure percentages, while barring public publication; however, a failing model is no longer required to stop selling, so withdrawal is left to regulator discretion. S5 removes the automatic numeric recall: the 8-per-100k threshold triggers review and notification only, and recall requires a regulator finding of serious risk or failed corrective action, which favours Halcyon's Ember 8. S3 and S4 favour Northwind on retrofit timing (6 years) and Halcyon on suppression timing (36 months)."
 },
